# 范蠡 (Fan Li) — top 12, reviewed

## Review of the top 10

1. **Change.** This is two rules welded together. The first (two gates) is really the first two channels of rule 5 — 天時 and 人事 *are* 與天 and 與人. The second (the 申胥 audience) is a different rule entirely: a sign of decay is not yet the decay. Keep only the first here and split the second out; both are promoted below, and the whole framework is merged into one algorithm at #1.
2. **Keep, extend.** The right rule, but it stops half a step. 國語 gives the other half immediately: 「得時不成，天有還形。天節不遠，五年復反，小凶則近，大凶則遠」 — if you get the moment and fail to finish, Heaven reverses and the window returns within five years. Merged in at #4. Also one factual slip: 玄月 is the **ninth** month (爾雅曰：「九月為玄」, and 韋昭 dates it to 魯哀十六年九月), not "the last month of the year."
3. **Change.** Right rule, sloppy quote. 「唯謀不遷」 quoted alone loses its subject; the actual clause is 「天節固然，唯謀不遷」 — Heaven's season is solid, *only the plan* does not shift. The contrast is the argument. Also 「夫十年謀之，一朝而棄之」 is the same rule a second time; one quote is enough. Promoted to #6.
4. **Keep, fix the quote.** The quote silently splices: the source reads 「…始於人者，人之所卒也；**淫佚之事，上帝之禁也，**先行此者，不利。」 The dropped clause is a separate charge (debauchery is forbidden by Heaven), not part of the "whoever begins it is destroyed by it" argument, and the cut is unmarked. The 史記 parallel 「試身於所末，上帝禁之，行者不利」 has no such gap. Promoted to #7.
5. **Change — merged into #1.** As written it is only the diagnostic half. Its own words 「有持盈，有定傾，有節事」 are immediately answered by 「持盈者與天，定傾者與人，節事者與地」, and then the *decision* half follows: 「天時不作，弗為人客；人事不起，弗為之始」. One framework, not two rules. The "How it decides" line is also the best in the top 10 — it shows the three answers being produced in order.
6. **Keep.** Clean, single-trigger, and correctly kept in 國語's wording rather than reconciled with 史記's. Promoted to #9.
7. **Change — this is the biggest rewrite.** It kept the labels and threw away the method. The passage says 「**用人無藝，往從其所**」 — 韋昭 glosses this as 「因敵為制，不豫設也」, *do not pre-set the method; take it from the enemy*. The top 10 dropped that clause and kept only 後則用陰／宜為人客, which are the labels, not the rule. It also dropped the three checks that actually gate an engagement (「必因天地之災」「又觀其民之飢飽勞逸以參之」「盡其陽節、盈吾陰節而奪之」) and the battlefield instruction 「彼來從我，固守勿與」. Rewritten at #8.
8. **Keep.** Best-shaped rule in the set: one trigger, one action, and he names his own weakness in his own mouth. Promoted to #10.
9. **Change — and it is a mindset, not a decision rule.** Three different moments merged: the warning letter (misjudge the ruler), 「君行令，臣行意」 (the servant's own will), and the Qi resignation (a commoner has reached his ceiling). They are one posture, but the top 10 never states the *reason* he gives first — 「今事已濟矣，蠡請從會稽之罰」: the debt was incurred in hardship and is discharged when the work is done. Also a sourcing defect: 「君行**令**，臣行意」 is 史記/卷41. 國語/卷21 reads 「君行**制**，臣行意」 (韋昭: 制，法也；意，志也). The source line lists both under one heading, so the string checks out in 史記 and the error is invisible. Rewritten as one mindset at #5.
10. **Drop from the top 12, keep in the file.** This is the weakest-attributed rule of the ten: none of it is in his voice. 「與時逐而不責於人」 and 「十九年之中三致千金」 are 史記's narrator in 貨殖列傳; the doctrine itself is 計然's (「知斗則修備，時用則知物…財幣欲其行如流水」), and the research says so correctly in its Gaps. 「此天下之中，交易有無之路通」 is also 史記's narrator. Nothing here is a *decision* he is recorded making — it is a biography's judgement of a career. If the seat ever needs commerce rules, re-promote 「與時逐而不責於人。故善治生者，能擇人而任時」 (史記/卷129) as a personnel rule: choose the people, then use the timing.

## What the top 10 missed

- **What you do while you wait.** The top 10 says "wait" six times and never once says what to *do* during the wait. 國語 answers it directly: 「時不至，不可彊生；事不究，不可彊成。**自若以處，以度天下，待其來者而正之，因時之所宜而定之。**…**事無閒，時無反，則撫民保教以須之**」 — make no forced move, measure everything, fix what the season fixes, and if no turn comes, govern and protect the people until it does. The research noticed 「無曠其眾，以為亂梯」 and filed it in Gaps; it is half of a larger answer it did not see. Promoted to #2 — for a seat whose whole job is "is it the right time?", this is the most useful thing he says.
- **The omen is not the thing.** 「逆節萌生。天地未形，而先為之征，其事是以不成，雜受其刑。」 He refuses when the evidence looks *best* — the enemy has just executed its best minister, which is the clearest possible sign. The visible sign is a 征, a symptom; the form has not appeared. Promoted to #3.
- **Do not pre-set the method.** See review of #7. 「用人無藝，往從其所」 is the operative rule and it was cut.
- **The criterion for a good victory.** 「是故戰勝而不報，取地而不反，兵勝於外，福生於內，用力甚少而名聲章明」 — win so there is nothing to come back for, take ground without needing to return it, win outside so the inside grows, spend almost nothing and let the reputation announce itself. The top 10 has rules about *when* to fight and *how* to fight and none about what counts as a win. Promoted to #11.
- **Making yourself smaller than the other side's rhetoric.** 「余雖靦然而人面哉，吾猶禽獸也，又安知是諓諓者乎？」 — he answers 吴's envoy by denying he can understand language, so the envoy has nothing to report. Then: 「君王已委制於執事之人矣。子往矣，無使執事之人得罪於子」 — release the envoy unharmed so he is not punished for carrying the refusal. Then he does not re-consult the king at all: 「范蠡不報於王，擊鼓興師以隨使者」. A communication procedure, entirely absent. Promoted to #12.
- **「臣聞之」 as a stance.** Six times in 國語/卷21 he opens with 臣聞之, 臣聞古之善用兵者, 臣聞命矣. He never says "I think"; he says "I heard it." It is a genuine epistemic habit — he executes transmitted doctrine rather than claiming invention — and it is the mechanism behind his best quote about the economy (the doctrine is 計然's, not his). Left out of the 12 because it never changes a decision on its own; it is the frame, not the rule.
- **Send the hard job to whoever has known hardship.** 「彼非不愛其弟，顧有所不能忍者也…至如少弟者，生而見我富，乘堅驅良逐狡兔，豈知財所從來，故輕棄之」 (史記/卷41). The research filed it in Gaps as well-sourced but "not a war or money rule" — it is a selection rule, and the seat has one. Also from Gaps: 「無曠其眾，以為亂梯」, now at #2.
- **Independent sources the research did not check.** It said no independent source was consulted for 越絕書/吳越春秋. 吳越春秋·勾踐歸國外傳第八 (勾踐九年) gives a Fan Li strategy that is *not* in 國語 or 史記 and is not the wait-for-the-moment strategy: 「臣請按師整兵，待其壞敗，隨而襲之，兵不血刃，士不旋踵。臣願大王匿聲無見其動，以觀其靜」 — sit on the army until their structure fails, then take them without blood, and hide your own movements while you do. The same chapter has 「外郭築城而缺西北，示服事吳也，不敢壅塞，內以取吳，故缺西北，而吳不知也」 — build the capital with a deliberate gap facing the overlord, which reads as submission and is actually the hole you will expand through. Both `attributed`, from a ~2nd-century text whose chronology conflicts with 史記. Not promoted: too late to sit beside 國語 on equal footing, but worth knowing it exists.
- **The persona.** 史記三家註·正義 quoting 會稽典錄: 「范蠡字少伯…本是楚宛三戶人，**佯狂倜儻負俗**」, and 文種's report of him: 「范蠡本國狂人，生有此病」 — answered with 「吾聞士有賢俊之姿，必有佯狂之譏，內懷獨見之明，外有不知之毀」. Inner clarity, outer apparent madness. That is the register 國語's 「吾猶禽獸也」 is written in, so it corroborates #12 rather than standing alone.

## Top 12

1. **Kind:** algorithm
   **In plain English:** Every situation has one of three forms — holding the full, steadying the leaning, ordering affairs — and each is answered by a different authority: the full follows Heaven, the leaning follows people, affairs follow the ground. Then two gates decide your role: if Heaven's timing has not ripened, do not be the attacker; if human conditions have not risen, do not be the initiator. If both are ripe, you are the attacker and you go.
   **Their words:** 「夫國家之事，有持盈，有定傾，有節事。」/「持盈者與天，定傾者與人，節事者與地。」/「夫聖人隨時以行，是謂守時。天時不作，弗為人客；人事不起，弗為之始。」 — "Matters of state have three forms: holding the full, steadying the leaning, ordering affairs." / "To hold the full, accord with Heaven; to steady the leaning, accord with people; to order affairs, accord with the ground." / "The sage moves with the season; that is keeping the season. When Heaven's timing does not arise, do not be the guest [attacker]; when human conditions do not arise, do not be the one who begins."
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §1 「范蠡進諫句踐持盈定傾節事」, the exchange beginning 「王曰：為三者，奈何？」 — Wikisource 國語/卷21. Variant in 史記/卷041: 「持滿者與天，定傾者與人，節事者以地」.
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** top-10 #1 and #5 merged

2. **Kind:** algorithm
   **In plain English:** The steps for waiting. (1) Do not force what is not yet in season. (2) Stay as you are — no improvised moves. (3) Measure everything while you wait. (4) Fix what the season says should be fixed, nothing else. (5) Put the people to work — open the fields, fill the granaries — and never leave anyone idle, because idle people become the ladder disorder climbs. (6) If no opening and no turn, govern and protect and keep waiting.
   **Their words:** 「時不至，不可彊生；事不究，不可彊成。自若以處，以度天下，待其來者而正之，因時之所宜而定之。同男女之功，除民之害，以避天殃。田野開闢，府倉實，民眾殷。無曠其眾，以為亂梯。…事無閒，時無反，則撫民保教以須之。」 — "When the season has not come, do not force growth; when the matter is not exhausted, do not force completion. Be as you are, measure the world, and when it comes, set it right; fix what is fixed by the season. Do men's and women's work, remove the people's harms, avoid Heaven's punishment. Open the fields, fill the granaries, make the people numerous. Never leave your people idle, or idleness becomes the ladder of disorder… If there is no opening and no turn, then govern the people, protect and teach them, and wait."
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §1, the answer to 「王問於范蠡曰：節事奈何？」
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** new

3. **Kind:** decision rule
   **In plain English:** A visible sign that the enemy is decaying is not the decay. Rebellion and disorder only *sprout*; until Heaven and Earth have taken their actual form, acting on the sign is what makes the enterprise fail and is what brings the punishment on you.
   **Their words:** 「逆節萌生。天地未形，而先為之征，其事是以不成，雜受其刑。王姑待之。」 — "Inverted discipline is sprouting. Heaven and Earth have not yet taken form, and you act first on the symptom — that is why the affair does not succeed, and you take the penalty along with it. For now, wait."
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §4 「范蠡謂先為之征其事不成」, in answer to the news that 申胥 was killed for repeated remonstrance.
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** new (the second rule inside top-10 #1)

4. **Kind:** decision rule
   **In plain English:** When the moment arrives, everything at once — the whole army, that season, before the window closes. And the corollary: if the moment arrived and you did not finish, Heaven reverses and the window comes back within five years, closer for a small disaster and farther for a great one. So the urgency is real but it is not panic.
   **Their words:** 「臣聞從時者，猶救火、追亡人也，蹶而趨之，唯恐弗及。」/「得時無怠，時不再來，天予不取，反為之災。」/「得時不成，天有還形。天節不遠，五年復反，小凶則近，大凶則遠。」 — "To follow the moment is like fighting a fire or chasing a fugitive: run and press, fearing only that you arrive too late." / "With the moment obtained, do not slacken; the moment does not come twice. What Heaven gives and you do not take turns into a disaster." / "If the moment is obtained and the work is not done, Heaven has a shape in which to turn it back. Heaven's season is not far; it returns within five years — near for a small ill, far for a great one."
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §6 「越興師伐吳而弗與戰」 (first two) and §7 「范蠡諫句踐勿許吳成卒滅吳」 (third).
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** top-10 #2, extended

5. **Kind:** mindset
   **In plain English:** Your obligation to a ruler is incurred in hardship and discharged when the work is done — not renewed by success. So: the ruler who shared your hardship will not share your triumph; a high name is a place of danger; and to hold an honoured name for long is unlucky. This is why he leaves, and it is a standing judgement he applies to himself before anyone offers him anything.
   **Their words:** 「臣聞之，為人臣者，君憂臣勞，君辱臣死…今事已濟矣，蠡請從會稽之罰。」/「蜚鳥盡，良弓藏；狡兔死，走狗烹。越王為人長頸鳥喙，可與共患難，不可與共樂。子何不去？」/「范蠡以為大名之下，難以久居」/「居家則致千金，居官則至卿相，此布衣之極也。久受尊名，不祥。」 — "I have heard: of a ruler's servant, when the ruler worries the servant labours, when the ruler is humiliated the servant dies… now the matter is accomplished, I ask to answer for the punishment of 會稽." / "When the birds are gone the good bow is stored; when the cunning hare is dead the hunting dog is cooked. The King of Yue is long-necked and bird-beaked: he can share hardship with you, not happiness. Why do you not leave?" / "Fan Li considered that beneath a great name it is hard to stay long." / "At home you reach a thousand gold; in office the rank of minister — that is the limit of a commoner. To hold an honoured name for long is unlucky."
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §8 「范蠡乘輕舟以浮於五湖」 (first, with 「君行制，臣行意」); 史記/卷041, 范蠡 section (letter to 文種, 「大名之下」, and the Qi resignation).
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** top-10 #9, rewritten

6. **Kind:** decision rule
   **In plain English:** Heaven's season is solid; only the plan shifts, and it does not. A plot settled in the ancestral temple is not re-opened on the plain — and years of preparation are not thrown away for one day of feeling.
   **Their words:** 「天節固然，唯謀不遷。」/「夫謀之廊廟，失之中原，其可乎？王姑勿許也。」 — "Heaven's season is of course solid; only the plan does not shift." / "A plot lost in the ancestral temple and lost again on the plain — is that permissible? For now, do not agree to it."
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §6, said when Wu challenged five times in one day and the king could not bear it; 韋昭 on 唯謀不遷: 「謀必素定，不可遷易」. 史記/卷041 has the doctrine without these words: 「謀之二十二年，一旦而棄之，可乎？」
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** top-10 #3, requoted

7. **Kind:** decision rule
   **In plain English:** Force is the last thing in affairs, not the first. Attacking is against virtue, weapons are lethal instruments, secret plotting is against virtue, whoever begins against a man is destroyed by him, and doing it first is not to your advantage. Debauchery is separately forbidden by Heaven.
   **Their words:** 「夫勇者，逆德也；兵者，凶器也；爭者，事之末也。陰謀逆德，好用凶器，始於人者，人之所卒也；淫佚之事，上帝之禁也，先行此者，不利。」 — "Courage that attacks is against virtue; weapons are lethal instruments; contention is the last thing in affairs. To plot secretly is against virtue, to use lethal instruments; whoever begins against a man is destroyed by him; debauchery is a thing Heaven forbids; to do this first is not to your advantage."
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §1, second audience, immediately before the army loses at 五湖 and takes refuge at 會稽. 史記/卷041: 「臣聞兵者凶器也，戰者逆德也，爭者事之末也…試身於所末，上帝禁之，行者不利」.
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** top-10 #4, un-spliced

8. **Kind:** algorithm
   **In plain English:** Do not pre-set the method — take it from the opponent. Steps: (1) If they come to you, hold and do not engage. (2) If you must engage, require three things together — a Heaven-sent disaster, and their people hungry or tired — and take the measure of all three. (3) Wait until their yang is spent and your own yin is full, then take. (4) When it suits you to attack: hard and fast, and do not expect to take them while their yang is unspent. When it suits you to defend: calm, slow, solid, and unforceable while their yin is unspent. (5) Deploy so that your formation follows theirs.
   **Their words:** 「用人無藝，往從其所」/「彼來從我，固守勿與。若將與之，必因天地之災，又觀其民之飢飽勞逸以參之。盡其陽節、盈吾陰節而奪之。宜為人客，剛彊而力疾；陽節不盡，輕而不可取。宜為人主，安徐而重固；陰節不盡，柔而不可迫。」 — "In employing men there is no fixed rule; go and follow where they are." / "If they come to me, hold fast and do not join battle. If you are going to join them, it must be because of a Heaven-sent disaster, and you must weigh in their people's hunger, fullness, labour and ease. Only when their yang season is spent and your own yin season is full do you take it." / "When it suits you to be the guest [attacker], be fierce and fast; while their yang is not yet spent, do not attack lightly and expect to take them. When it suits you to be the host, be calm, slow and solid; while their yin is not yet spent, soft though they are, they cannot be forced." — 韋昭 on 用人無藝: 「因敵為制，不豫設也」
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §6, the whole 臣聞古之善用兵者 passage.
   **Label:** `quoted` (the gloss 因敵為制 is `attributed` to 韋昭, c. 3rd c. CE)
   **From:** top-10 #7, rewritten

9. **Kind:** decision rule
   **In plain English:** When you are losing, buy peace by putting yourself on the table, not the country. Humble your words, honour their ritual, give treasures and singing-girls, dignify them with titles. If that does not end it, put your own person in the market — that is, go as servant, hand over the state seals and keys, and give your women as their wives. Not the territory.
   **Their words:** 「卑辭尊禮，玩好女樂，尊之以名。如此不已，又身與之市。」 — "Humble your words, honour their ritual; offer treasures and singing-girls, dignify them with titles. If it does not stop at that, then put your person on the market." — 韋昭: 「市，利也，謂委管籥屬國家，以身隨之」
   **Source:** 國語/卷21 §1, given to the king *after* the army had already lost at 五湖 and was besieged at 會稽. 史記/卷041: 「卑辭厚禮以遺之，不許，而身與之市」.
   **Label:** `quoted`
   **From:** top-10 #6, kept

10. **Kind:** decision rule
    **In plain English:** Give every job to the person better at it — including the jobs you are better at — and say so out loud. He names himself the wrong man for governing his own country and asks for the external and military command instead. And the deeper version, from the son's death: send the hard job to whoever has known hardship, because the person raised comfortable does not know where the money came from and so spends it lightly.
    **Their words:** 「四封之內，百姓之事，蠡不如種也。四封之外，敵國之制，立斷之事，種亦不如蠡也。」/「兵甲之事，種不如蠡；填撫國家，親附百姓，蠡不如種。」/「彼非不愛其弟，顧有所不能忍者也…至如少弟者，生而見我富，乘堅驅良逐狡兔，豈知財所從來，故輕棄之」 — "Inside the four borders, the people's business: I am not as good as 種. Outside the four borders, the enemy's pressure and the decisive stroke: 種 is not as good as I am." / "Arms and armour: 種 is not as good as I am; settling and cherishing the state, winning the people: I am not as good as 種." / "It is not that he did not love his brother; it is that there was something he could not bear. …As for the younger son, born to see me rich, riding firm chariots and driving good horses chasing cunning hares — how would he know where the wealth came from, and so he values it lightly and spends it."
    **Source:** 國語/卷21 §1 (in answer to 「王曰：蠡為我守於國」, and again when the king offers him the whole state); 史記/卷041, 范蠡 section (compact form; the son). The son's speech is 史記's record of what he said, built on the 莊生 anecdote — see Gaps.
    **Label:** `quoted` (the son passage is `attributed`)
    **From:** top-10 #8, extended with the research's own Gaps item

11. **Kind:** decision rule
    **In plain English:** Judge a victory by whether it can be left alone. Win so the enemy cannot strike back, take ground so you need not give it back, win outside so that blessing grows inside — and spend as little as possible, letting the fame announce itself.
    **Their words:** 「是故戰勝而不報，取地而不反，兵勝於外，福生於內，用力甚少而名聲章明，種亦不如蠡也。」 — "Therefore to win a battle and have no repayment come, to take land and not have to give it back: to win in arms outside and have fortune arise within; to use very little force and have the reputation become manifest."
    **Source:** 國語/卷21 §1, the closing clause of his answer on 四封之外, immediately before 「王曰：諾。令大夫種為之。」 He hands this part to 文種, which is why it is easy to miss.
    **Label:** `quoted`
    **From:** new

12. **Kind:** decision rule
    **In plain English:** When you are the weaker party and the other side has the better rhetoric, make yourself smaller than their argument: disclaim the ability to understand it, so there is nothing to report back. Release their messenger unharmed so he is not punished for carrying your refusal. Then decide on the spot and do not go back to the king — raise the drum and follow the envoy out.
    **Their words:** 「余雖靦然而人面哉，吾猶禽獸也，又安知是諓諓者乎？」/「君王已委制於執事之人矣。子往矣，無使執事之人得罪於子。」/「范蠡不報於王，擊鼓興師以隨使者。」 — "Though I have a human face, I am ashamed of it; I am still a beast — how would I know anything about this glib talk?" / "The king has already committed the matter into the hands of the officer in charge. Go your way; do not let the officer in charge be put in the wrong by you." / "Fan Li did not report back to the king; he beat the drum, raised the army and followed the envoy."
    **Source:** 國語/卷21 §7 「范蠡諫句踐勿許吳成卒滅吳」.
    **Label:** `quoted`
    **From:** new

## Gaps

- **The design's own Fan Li quote is not his.** design.md line 29 gives 「時不至，不可強生；事不究，不可強成」 to 國語·越語下. It is in 國語/卷21, but **inside 韋昭's note on 節事者與地** — the wikitext reads 「節事者與地。{{*|與地，法地也。時不至不可彊生，事不究不可彊成之屬。}}」. Those are a third-century CE commentator's words, glossing 與地, and 范蠡 does not speak them. The quote-check confirmed the characters are present in the named source, which is exactly the limit of what it was written to establish. If that line goes into a seat, it must be labelled 韋昭, not 范蠡.
- **Verification method.** I re-fetched Wikisource 國語/卷21, 史記/卷041, 史記/卷129, 吳越春秋/勾踐歸國外傳, 史記三家註/卷041 and 越絕書/卷14 and tested every clause above against the source text with the glosses stripped and variant characters normalised. Every clause in the Top 12 matched its named source. Two strings I had to correct from the research's wording rather than from the source: 「君行令」 (史記) vs 「君行制」 (國語), and the 玄月 date. All of these are Wikisource re-editions with no critical apparatus — a Zhonghua 史記 remains the final check, as the research said.
- **ctext.org still blocked**, as in the original run. 史記正義 (which carries 會稽典錄) is available on Wikisource and is how I sourced the 佯狂 material; a Zhonghua edition of the 集解/索隱/正義 triple would be better.
- **越絕書: partially checked, and it is not neutral.** I read 卷十四 (越絕德序外傳記第十八) and found three things worth a line — 「若卑辭以地讓之」 (cede the land as well as the person, a variant of #9), 「范蠡內視若盲，反聽若聾，度天關，涉天機」, and 「貴微而賤獲」. The same chapter says 「范蠡恐懼，逃於五湖」, which flatly contradicts the deliberate, reasoned exit in 國語 §8 and 史記 — a reason to treat the text's 序 as late and unreliable rather than as evidence. **I could not read 越絕書 卷1–13 or 15**: the fetches were refused, so I cannot claim there is no other 范蠡 material there. Worth one more pass.
- **吳越春秋 was not usable as equal evidence.** The 兵不血刃 and 缺西北 passages are real and verified, but 吳越春秋 is ~2nd c. CE, its campaign chronology conflicts with 史記, and 韋昭 is citing it by a chapter name ("某則") rather than quoting it — so it is being used as corroboration of later readers, not as a text of the 春秋 period.
- **Two late, uncorroborated sources I deliberately did not use.** 無能子/范蠡說 (Tang) gives 「吾聞陰謀人者，其禍必復」 and a long exchange in which 文種 argues that removing a menace is not the same as sinning against Heaven — good, but a Tang fictional dialogue with no manuscript pedigree I could check. 春秋戰國異辭 (late Qing) carries a farewell speech not in 國語 or 史記 — 「臣聞君子俟時計，不數謀；死不被疑，內不自欺」 — which would be a genuinely new item if true, but the page returned a redirect and I could not verify the text. Both are named here so a later run can decide.
- **史記's son-in-Chu speech stays `attributed`.** It is built on the 莊生 anecdote and is 史記's record of what he said, not a transcript. I have kept it inside #10 rather than standing it alone, so nothing depends on it.
- **未收於十二 but real, in case the seat is re-scoped:** 「善治生者，能擇人而任時」 (史記/卷129 — choose the people, then use the timing); 「王乃遣工以良金寫范蠡之狀而朝禮之，環會稽三百里者以為范蠡地」 (國語 §8 — the state wrote his image in gold and made him a hereditary fief, which is the other half of #5 and complicates it); 「持盈者與天…節事者與地」的 史記 variant 以地 for 與地, still unreconciled.
